#24: 
kzalloc might cause sleep and will generate some warning detected by lockdep,

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*trigger)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct led_trigger)...)
#64: FILE: drivers/leds/led-triggers.c:258:
+	trigger = kzalloc(sizeof(struct led_trigger), GFP_ATOMIC);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

